{"seconds": 60.7, "exit": 0, "final": "Okay, so the line is:\n1. **Nh6+** - driving the king\n2. **Kh8** (best try; if Kf8 or Kg7 similar)  \n3. **Bf6+** - forcing Rg7\n4. **Rg7** (forced)\n5. **Bxg7+** - winning the exchange\n6. **Kxg7**\n7. **Nf5+** - winning further with a strong attack\n\nThis is a clear forcing sequence winning material and delivering a devastating attack. The motif is a combination of **fork** (the knight repeatedly forks the king and other pieces) and **attraction** (forcing the king into worse squares).\n\n**Coaching note:** The key insight is recognizing that after Nh6+ forces Kh8, the follow-up Bf6+ creates an unstoppable mating attack. The rook is trapped and must go to g7, allowing Bxg7+ followed by Nf5+, which wins decisively. Always look for forcing checks that limit your opponent's options and create multiple threats.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nh6+\", \"line\": [\"Nh6+\", \"Kh8\", \"Bf6+\", \"Rg7\", \"Bxg7+\", \"Kxg7\", \"Nf5+\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"attraction\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "6k1/2r2N1p/p3p1p1/8/2B3PB/1P2Q3/P4K1P/3r3q w - - 3 33"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "6k1/2r2N1p/p3p1p1/8/2B3PB/1P2Q3/P4K1P/3r3q w - - 3 33"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "6k1/2r2N1p/p3p1p1/8/2B3PB/1P2Q3/P4K1P/3r3q w - - 3 33"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "6k1/2r2N1p/p3p1p1/8/2B3PB/1P2Q3/P4K1P/3r3q w - - 3 33", "move": "Nh6+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "6k1/2r4p/p3p1pN/8/2B3PB/1P2Q3/P4K1P/3r3q b - - 4 33", "move": "Kh8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "7k/2r4p/p3p1pN/8/2B3PB/1P2Q3/P4K1P/3r3q w - - 5 34", "move": "Nf7+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "7k/2r2N1p/p3p1p1/8/2B3PB/1P2Q3/P4K1P/3r3q b - - 6 34", "move": "Rxf7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "7k/2r2N1p/p3p1p1/8/2B3PB/1P2Q3/P4K1